  <text class="dg-lbl" x="520" y="272">WHAT HAD CHANGED SINCE 1986</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="520" y="298">BACKPROPAGATION WAS PUBLISHED IN 1986, AND CONVOLUTIONAL</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="520" y="312">NETWORKS READ POSTAL DIGITS BY THE LATE 1980s. NOTHING IN</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="520" y="326">THIS WAS NEW IN 2012 EXCEPT ITS FEASIBILITY.</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="520" y="354">— LABELLED DATA IN QUANTITIES NOBODY HAD PREVIOUSLY HAD</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="520" y="372">— GRAPHICS PROCESSORS SUITED TO DENSE MATRIX ARITHMETIC</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="520" y="390">— RECTIFIED LINEAR UNITS AND DROPOUT, WHICH MADE DEEP</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-key" x="536" y="404">STACKS TRAINABLE</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="520" y="432">A RARE CASE OF A THEORY WAITING DECADES FOR ITS INPUTS</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-soft" x="520" y="446">RATHER THAN THE OTHER WAY ROUND.</text>
  <text class="dg-lbl dg-num" x="520" y="468">60 MILLION PARAMETERS · 1.2 MILLION IMAGES</text>
